# denoisetvd

- Label: Denoise TVD
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 3
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/denoisetvd.html
- Summary (EN): Removes white noise by reducing curvature in the image heightfield representation, eliminating high-frequency specks while preserving sharp edges better than a blur. Distinct from Denoise AI.
- Résumé (FR) : Supprime le bruit blanc par diffusion de courbure, en gardant les bords nets mais en effaçant les détails fins.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to denoise", "speed: optional mono layer varying denoising speed per pixel; multiplies Speed and should stay below one", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: mix of new and original value; default 1 uses only the new value and sets the affected RGBA channels", "Iterations: number of denoising rounds; more removes more noise and more detail, with runtime scaling", "Speed: diffusion per round; total diffusion equals Speed multiplied by Iterations"]

- Caveats: ["Texture detail is treated as noise and suppressed.", "A high Speed can make the process unstable and prevent convergence."]

